============================================================
STEP 19 - RESULT REVEAL + DEFINED CEILING DIAGNOSIS
============================================================

Reveal the target result.

Calculate actual EH/H/W/C.

Report:

- predicted/frozen profile;
- actual profile;
- exact profile YES/NO;
- each winner's immediate-transition family;
- actual transition rank in each pool;
- actual canonical whole-scenario rank tuple;
- whether that exact scenario was selected;
- each winner's Independent Evidence rank;
- each winner's CandidateJoint rank;
- each winner's portfolio exposure;
- every winning same-family pair/group and whether it appeared;
- every winning cross-family pair and whether it appeared;
- each ticket's hits;
- hit distribution;
- maximum hit;
- tickets >=3, >=4, >=5, and 6/6;
- union coverage for diagnosis only.

Calculate ceilings EXACTLY as follows.

-------------------------
A. Profile Ceiling
-------------------------

Number of actual winners whose EH/H/W/C pool can be accommodated by PROFILE_FROZEN, respecting the frozen pool counts.

For each pool, at most the frozen count from that pool can survive.

Sum across pools.

-------------------------
B. Transition Scenario Ceiling
-------------------------

For every SELECTED scenario, calculate the maximum number of actual winners whose immediate-transition families can fit that scenario's exact family multiplicities.

This is a maximum bipartite/multiset fit problem inside each final pool.

Take the maximum across selected scenarios.

This ceiling can never exceed Profile Ceiling.

-------------------------
C. Candidate Exposure Ceiling
-------------------------

Starting from the best surviving selected scenario(s) from B, count only actual winners that:

1. fit that selected scenario's family multiplicities; AND
2. appeared at least once anywhere in the frozen 20-ticket portfolio in their correct immediate family.

Take the maximum achievable count across selected scenarios.

-------------------------
D. Same-Family Co-Location Ceiling
-------------------------

Starting from subsets that survive C:

For each immediate family independently, all selected actual winners from that family must have appeared TOGETHER in at least one frozen ticket.

Ignore cross-family relationships at this stage.

Find the largest surviving actual-winner subset satisfying that rule while remaining compatible with at least one selected scenario.

-------------------------
E. Cross-Family Assembly Ceiling
-------------------------

Starting from subsets that survive D:

For every pair of selected winners belonging to DIFFERENT immediate families, that exact pair must have co-occurred in at least one frozen ticket.

The cross-family pairs do NOT need to have occurred in the same historical/frozen ticket as each other for this diagnostic ceiling.

Find the largest surviving actual-winner subset satisfying:

- selected-scenario compatibility;
- candidate exposure;
- same-family group co-location;
- every required cross-family pair co-location.

This is the official V3 definition of Cross-Family Assembly Ceiling.

-------------------------
F. Final Ticket Hit
-------------------------

The largest number of actual winning main numbers contained in any ONE frozen ticket.

This is the actual portfolio result.

Report the chain:

`Profile Ceiling`
`-> Transition Scenario Ceiling`
`-> Candidate Exposure Ceiling`
`-> Same-Family Co-Location Ceiling`
`-> Cross-Family Assembly Ceiling`
`-> Final Ticket Hit`

Identify the FIRST stage where the ceiling falls.

Never blame a later layer for an earlier loss.

